{"statements": ["Entry‑level help‑desk positions look for a mix of basic technical abilities, customer‑service skills, and often some formal education or certifications.", "Basic Windows troubleshooting and familiarity with Microsoft Office/Outlook/Teams are required.", "Active Directory experience or working knowledge is required.", "Ability to reset passwords, support printers/scanners/copiers, and handle hardware (desktop/laptop) issues is required.", "Exposure to ticketing systems such as ServiceNow or other help‑desk tools is required.", "Optional/desired skills include SCCM/Autopilot deployment, Microsoft 365, networking basics, PowerShell, VPN, and SharePoint/OneDrive.", "Strong verbal and written communication and people skills for interacting with non‑technical users are required.", "Ability to stay calm and effective under pressure is required.", "Teamwork and remote‑work collaboration are required.", "Typically 1–2 years of help‑desk, call‑center, or related support experience is required.", "Some roles accept recent graduates or candidates with little experience but a willingness to learn.", "A high school diploma is the minimum education requirement.", "Many positions prefer an associate’s degree or college coursework in IT/IS.", "A+ certification is often strongly preferred or considered a bonus.", "CompTIA Network+ or other certifications are optional but advantageous.", "Work environment is mostly office‑based or remote with occasional on‑site days, e.g., 3 days per month.", "Full‑time schedule, often 8 am‑4 pm or similar, is typical."], "verdicts": [{"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict": "yes", "reason": null}, {"verdict":